 {:db/id "q-181806/field-3/7d149b60a8e2a3be02476cb4e4d26616193c2006082edf79693d6816cf527c19" :answer/id #uuid "9082c766-1bb5-5c2f-9b03-28a47e32ca5c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\le " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181806/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "13d53cde-b3f6-5fa1-8adc-3e0278a50e78" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-181806/field-3/e4e9dbe71f63d8d81739fdcbf2df64ccccd4c8f5d299ddc4b1c1f96031adb38e" :answer-field/choices ["q-181806/field-3/e4e9dbe71f63d8d81739fdcbf2df64ccccd4c8f5d299ddc4b1c1f96031adb38e" "q-181806/field-3/7d149b60a8e2a3be02476cb4e4d26616193c2006082edf79693d6816cf527c19"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-181806/field-4/e4e9dbe71f63d8d81739fdcbf2df64ccccd4c8f5d299ddc4b1c1f96031adb38e" :answer/id #uuid "664a10e5-3ce5-550c-a9d7-846c1b7088fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "<" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181806/field-4/7d149b60a8e2a3be02476cb4e4d26616193c2006082edf79693d6816cf527c19" :answer/id #uuid "734e0047-51aa-5137-b11a-92a9e6d42f84" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\le " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181806/field-4" :answer-field/id #uuid "4dfd3fb1-bf04-5acd-bc87-28038196ea05" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-181806/field-4/e4e9dbe71f63d8d81739fdcbf2df64ccccd4c8f5d299ddc4b1c1f96031adb38e" :answer-field/choices ["q-181806/field-4/e4e9dbe71f63d8d81739fdcbf2df64ccccd4c8f5d299ddc4b1c1f96031adb38e" "q-181806/field-4/7d149b60a8e2a3be02476cb4e4d26616193c2006082edf79693d6816cf527c19"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-181806" :question/id #uuid "06624e01-3e0b-5189-ac4c-e6d2964b1400" :question/math-academy-id "q-181806" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041529/assets/a659e2d14a645036488833cd920e6bb3e3d7a7716724dba63814be6df4066fe9.png)\n\nDescribe the shaded region shown above using set-builder notation.\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,3\\,{{field-1}}\\,x\\,{{field-2}}\\,6,\\,-1\\,{{field-3}}\\,y\\,{{field-4}}\\,4}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A point $P(x,y)$ lies *inside* the rectangle if the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3<x<6,\\,-1<y<4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we also need to *include* the left edge ($x=3$).\n\nTherefore, we change the corresponding inequality symbol to non-strict, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\le x<6,\\,-1<y<4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMoreover, since *every* real value in these intervals is included, $x\\in R,y\\in R,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\times R={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our set as follows:\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,3\\le x<6,\\,-1<y<4}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-181806/field-1" "q-181806/field-2" "q-181806/field-3" "q-181806/field-4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d9f0da82-f79b-5056-ac99-b401eb1630c7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-181806"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-181791/field-1/cfebd74d1bfcdc28a2ab76bc7b9cb134cbb44312ed3e16d5a0610048f75355ad" :answer/id #uuid "944a938a-a9ca-50b3-ab44-b411a71e3c2a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{N}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181791/field-1/904a9c19982d1c360bd0486a099ef7bc8a84d0ace236de1e1f77c56ca4d4caec" :answer/id #uuid "e154e61f-9f1b-534c-8277-2d0a793754e3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{Z}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181791/field-1/07d4d169afe54b72e6508fedd544e5d357fac0ff0f623249ab3b7f264f513fcf" :answer/id #uuid "7478a8db-a471-58a4-8c81-4f07290a0323" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181791/field-1/a1f44d584f3d5c0539cb338e6289ad49d176231f52c1da87f334282351fe2472" :answer/id #uuid "f44e086c-1ed5-5402-9b14-c