" "q-182024/field-1/07d4d169afe54b72e6508fedd544e5d357fac0ff0f623249ab3b7f264f513fcf" "q-182024/field-1/a1f44d584f3d5c0539cb338e6289ad49d176231f52c1da87f334282351fe2472"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-182024/field-2/cc57b3a2811193b1201e1d8d139011f0b8b63f9cad9aaf57f40ab2b8d40ee2eb" :answer/id #uuid "3fbccdd0-1406-5773-8ba4-ca606d840d0b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\ge " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-182024/field-2/22814de28a0b1b4f20d5edd62707d192b78050d457a70349795d30d86dfcd7fa" :answer/id #uuid "6636f95f-0dad-5883-a778-23224ede4872" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value ">" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-182024/field-2/7d149b60a8e2a3be02476cb4e4d26616193c2006082edf79693d6816cf527c19" :answer/id #uuid "f3a4e315-a9ef-5baf-a805-2b40c79aa7ab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\le " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-182024/field-2/55f4eef1ef55065220056c9644bf18d21761bc8db2d8f5c41f767a2fc9186b70" :answer/id #uuid "a76bc1ea-5e53-5187-aa36-c4c7a50c48f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\ne " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-182024/field-2/e4e9dbe71f63d8d81739fdcbf2df64ccccd4c8f5d299ddc4b1c1f96031adb38e" :answer/id #uuid "4e05d4a3-ad71-5fc3-b16b-b2967c9a87ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "<" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-182024/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "7b807db8-7eae-5042-8877-ca9e4368b55d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-182024/field-2/cc57b3a2811193b1201e1d8d139011f0b8b63f9cad9aaf57f40ab2b8d40ee2eb" :answer-field/choices ["q-182024/field-2/cc57b3a2811193b1201e1d8d139011f0b8b63f9cad9aaf57f40ab2b8d40ee2eb" "q-182024/field-2/22814de28a0b1b4f20d5edd62707d192b78050d457a70349795d30d86dfcd7fa" "q-182024/field-2/7d149b60a8e2a3be02476cb4e4d26616193c2006082edf79693d6816cf527c19" "q-182024/field-2/55f4eef1ef55065220056c9644bf18d21761bc8db2d8f5c41f767a2fc9186b70" "q-182024/field-2/e4e9dbe71f63d8d81739fdcbf2df64ccccd4c8f5d299ddc4b1c1f96031adb38e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-182024" :question/id #uuid "29d1034a-32f8-58de-bfb9-996dde4c8c01" :question/math-academy-id "q-182024" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041529/assets/5adfe417126264290b9b49776a535e8ca27521a6bb13806df13bffe2807402fe.png)\n\nDescribe the shaded region shown above using set-builder notation.\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,x\\,{{field-2}}\\,-1}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Since all points $P(x,y)$ in our set lie at integer values of $x$ and $y,$ we have $x\\in Z,y\\in Z,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in Z\\times Z={Z}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe points in our set include all those that lie *to the right* the line $x=-1.$ For those points, the following condition is satisfied:\n\n$$\nx>-1\n$$\n\nAlso, notice that some points in our set lie *on* the line. We include these points by changing the inequality symbol above as follows:\n\n$$\nx\\ge -1\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as follows:\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {Z}^{2}\\,:\\,x\\ge -1}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-182024/field-1" "q-182024/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e694b201-5ec6-5cc3-a608-2447d1cc1ed3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-182024"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186195330 :answer-field/correct 17592186195334 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186195336 :answer-field/correct 17592186195340 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186195324 :answer-field/correct 17592186195325 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-181678"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041529/assets/0f95f6b259237816a5a3da041452cfd9458f0852b1ae717a044738b6f310ab5d.png)\n\nDescribe the shaded region shown above using set-builder notation.\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,3\\,{{field-2}}\\,y\\,{{field-3}}\\,2x+3}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The points in our set include all those that lie *above* the line $y=3$ and *below* the line $y=2x+3.$\n\nA point $P(x,y)$ lies *inside* the shaded region if the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n$$\ny>3,\\,y<2x+3.\n$$\n\nCombining this into a single condition, we have\n\n$$\n3<y<2x+3.\n$$\n\nWe must also include the lines $y=3$ and $y=2x+3$ since the boundaries are included in the set (the lines are solid). So, we change the corresponding inequality symbols above as follows:\n\n$$\n3\\le y\\le 2x+3\n$$\n\nMoreover, since we're considering *every* real value in this region, $x\\in R,y\\in R,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\times R={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,3\\le y\\le 2x+3}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-181682/field-1/5fc5100246d98d57a3a3e1d40181b00e6e8dff5d4a097ce2d7b7f6ae0b08578e" :answer/id #uuid "b70a1237-3df1-5d61-aa9a-33d2170f1170" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181682/field-1/07d4d169afe54b72e6508fedd544e5d357fac0ff0f623249ab3b7f264f513fcf" :answer/id #uuid "8e97f100-9a3e-5689-9815-78204f49e79f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181682/field-1/203f88d94a38bb859e78e84aea518cf34952815758cf391887040455367d62ef" :answer/id #uuid "075c0b5b-f8e9-5ec7-a79f-4c0606238509" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "N" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181682/field-1/a1f44d584f3d5c0539cb338e6289ad49d176231f52c1da87f334282351fe2472" :answer/id #uuid "56f6cf5f-5fd7-552f-8266-ba7477ec6413" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "R" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181682/field-1/62fc74d0eb6ece7bf9beb52d92d3e5dd4c591eb0e1df3eb95bec