b78050d457a70349795d30d86dfcd7fa" :answer/id #uuid "dd07241d-1c46-53a2-955b-b98455bd57b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value ">" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181686/field-3/7d149b60a8e2a3be02476cb4e4d26616193c2006082edf79693d6816cf527c19" :answer/id #uuid "ac654187-6596-5b43-ae1e-1d351a51c765" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\le " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181686/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "62de761f-a064-5cd2-9f41-18256c9b8e0d" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-181686/field-3/7d149b60a8e2a3be02476cb4e4d26616193c2006082edf79693d6816cf527c19" :answer-field/choices ["q-181686/field-3/e4e9dbe71f63d8d81739fdcbf2df64ccccd4c8f5d299ddc4b1c1f96031adb38e" "q-181686/field-3/cc57b3a2811193b1201e1d8d139011f0b8b63f9cad9aaf57f40ab2b8d40ee2eb" "q-181686/field-3/55f4eef1ef55065220056c9644bf18d21761bc8db2d8f5c41f767a2fc9186b70" "q-181686/field-3/22814de28a0b1b4f20d5edd62707d192b78050d457a70349795d30d86dfcd7fa" "q-181686/field-3/7d149b60a8e2a3be02476cb4e4d26616193c2006082edf79693d6816cf527c19"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-181686" :question/id #uuid "e9df87e0-0717-52c5-9ed8-9a7d72fd2a04" :question/math-academy-id "q-181686" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041529/assets/67eeabfcff4eb24e14c15691c1c9de746a8870808197739577f7696faeada5bc.png)\n\nDescribe the shaded region shown above using set-builder notation.\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,y\\,{{field-2}}\\,4,\\,y\\,{{field-3}}\\,4x+1}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The points in our set include all those that lie *below* the line $y=4$ and *below* the line $y=4x+1.$\n\nA point $P(x,y)$ lies *inside* the shaded region if the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n$$\ny<4,\\,y<4x+1.\n$$\n\nWe must also include the lines $y=4$ and $y=4x+1$ since the boundaries are included in the set (the lines are solid). So, we change the corresponding inequality symbols above as follows:\n\n$$\ny\\le 4,\\,y\\le 4x+1\n$$\n\nMoreover, since we're considering *every* real value in this region, $x\\in R,y\\in R,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\times R={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y\\le 4,\\,y\\le 4x+1}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-181686/field-1" "q-181686/field-2" "q-181686/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a3df69f-653e-5148-bd46-580097e43362"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-181686"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-181685/field-1/a1f44d584f3d5c0539cb338e6289ad49d176231f52c1da87f334282351fe2472" :answer/id #uuid "319c5a85-9877-5a84-81ce-eab67aad58ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "R" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181685/field-1/5fc5100246d98d57a3a3e1d40181b00e6e8dff5d4a097ce2d7b7f6ae0b08578e" :answer/id #uuid "41589387-c8b1-5857-8fd2-e305f0cf3ffb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181685/field-1/203f88d94a38bb859e78e84aea518cf34952815758cf391887040455367d62ef" :answer/id #uuid "bb8b1dcd-1510-55ae-add0-7cd0ce9d1517" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "N" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181685/field-1/07d4d169afe54b72e6508fedd544e5d357fac0ff0f623249ab3b7f264f513fcf" :answer/id #uuid "517cde0f-a020-59b5-b37a-804548b2826f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181685/field-1/62fc74d0eb6ece7bf9beb52d92d3e5dd4c591eb0e1df3eb95bec90a49e0fa322" :answer/id #uuid "518a4e21-8195-5247-9eee-2a6e9865ae79" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{C}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-181685/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "63cbd75e-3c3d-5d91-aa72-61bb4e9f6bba" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-1