ield-3/22814de28a0b1b4f20d5edd62707d192b78050d457a70349795d30d86dfcd7fa" "q-181685/field-3/e4e9dbe71f63d8d81739fdcbf2df64ccccd4c8f5d299ddc4b1c1f96031adb38e" "q-181685/field-3/55f4eef1ef55065220056c9644bf18d21761bc8db2d8f5c41f767a2fc9186b70" "q-181685/field-3/cc57b3a2811193b1201e1d8d139011f0b8b63f9cad9aaf57f40ab2b8d40ee2eb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-181685" :question/id #uuid "f331ef54-bc51-59b8-90bd-d826303b3fd7" :question/math-academy-id "q-181685" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041529/assets/f2d1c647ec7899221567d67e24e90a9f1efca60650b82a739e843e4085be636e.png)\n\nDescribe the shaded region shown above using set-builder notation.\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {{field-1}}\\,:\\,2x\\,{{field-2}}\\,y\\,{{field-3}}\\,-x+3}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The points in our set include all those that lie *above* the line $y=2x$ and *below* the line $y=-x+3.$\n\nA point $P(x,y)$ lies *inside* the shaded region if the following conditions are satisfied:\n\n$$\ny>2x,\\,y<-x+3.\n$$\n\n \n\nCombining this into a single condition, we have\n\n$$\n2x<y<-x+3.\n$$\n\n \n\nSince the boundary is not included in the set (the lines are dashed), the inequalities are strict.\n\nMoreover, since we're considering *every* real value in this region, $x\\in R,y\\in R,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in R\\times R={R}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as\n\n$$\n{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,2x<y<-x+3}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-181685/field-1" "q-181685/field-2" "q-181685/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a3df69f-653e-5148-bd46-580097e43362"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-181685"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-181691/field-1/7d512723ec7933fc53d818fe067378407b0cca1985b020babe9fcffa79cfd32b" :answer/id #uuid "73cedf0c-5740-540a-933f-49ccc34134c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :